# dp_exchange_schwab — environment variable template.
#
# This is the ONLY .env file that is committed. `.gitignore` carries
# `.env*` / `!.env.sample`; every other .env is yours and stays local.
#
#     cp .env.sample .env
#
# Secrets live in .env files and nowhere else. There is no `config/*.secret.exs` and no
# Vault layer.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# This repository holds no venue credential, and that is deliberate
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# The host obtains the grant. Schwab's initial authorisation is three-legged OAuth — a
# browser, a person, and a redirect through Schwab's login site — which no library can do.
# This package's half is credential *use*: it signs with an access token the caller passes
# per call, and `DpExchange.Schwab.refresh_credentials/2` exchanges a refresh token for a
# new one. It never obtains, stores or reads a credential of its own.
#
# So there is no Schwab app key or token here. Every endpoint on this venue needs one —
# market data included, since there is no anonymous surface — and there is no sandbox to
# point a credential-free test at either. Tier 1 (in-process fakes) is therefore all that
# runs unattended, and tiers 2 and 3 have nowhere to point until a credential-holding
# consumer runs them. A credential sitting in this public repository would be a liability
# with no upside.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Publishing
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Organisation key. CI publishes with the org secret; this is only for publishing by hand.
HEX_API_KEY=<your-hex-api-key>
